Dictionary
track_id / SongID: Unique identifier for the track (Spotify or MSD).
SongNumber: Index number for MSD entries.
Title / track_name: Name of the track.
AlbumID: Unique identifier for the album (MSD).
album_name: Name of the album on which the track appears.
ArtistID: Unique identifier for the performing artist.
artists / ArtistName: Name(s) of the artist(s) who performed the track.
mbID: MusicBrainz ID linking the track to external metadata.
popularity: A value between 0–100 measuring how frequently and recently a track has been streamed.
ArtistFamiliarity: A measure (0.0–1.0) estimating how well-known the artist is.
Hotness: A score capturing an artist or song’s cultural momentum or relevance.
duration_ms: The track length in milliseconds (Spotify).
Duration: Track length in seconds (MSD).
end_of_fade_in: Time (in seconds) when the fade-in section ends.
start_of_fade_out: Time (in seconds) when the fade-out begins.
key / KeySignature: The musical key using Pitch Class notation (0 = C, …, 11 = B).
keyConfidence / KeySignatureConfidence: Confidence (0.0–1.0) in key detection.
mode: Indicates major (1) or minor (0).
mode_confidence: Confidence score (0.0–1.0) for mode detection.
tempo: Estimated tempo in beats per minute (BPM).
TimeSignature: Estimated time signature, encoded as an integer (typically 3–7).
TimeSignatureConfidence: Confidence score (0.0–1.0) for time signature detection.
danceability: Describes how suitable a track is for dancing (0.0 = least, 1.0 = most).
energy: Perceptual intensity and activity of the track (0.0–1.0).
loudness / Loudness: Overall loudness level in decibels (dB).
speechiness: Measures presence of spoken words (0.0–1.0).
acousticness: Likelihood the track is acoustic (0.0–1.0).
instrumentalness: Probability the track contains no vocals (0.0–1.0).
liveness: Detects audience presence; values above 0.8 imply live performance.
valence: Musical positiveness (0.0 = sad, 1.0 = happy).

Documentation: 
Title:Integrated Audio Feature Dataset for Predicting Song Popularity

Description:
This dataset combines audio-feature data from the Spotify Tracks Dataset (Hugging Face) and a subset of the Million Song Dataset (Kaggle). The integrated dataset was created for an INFO 407 project examining whether song popularity can be predicted from audio characteristics alone. No personal or listener data is included.

Creators:
Zach Olbur, Dan Feder

Format:
CSV (primary dataset), PNG (visualizations)

Distributions:

CSV file containing all integrated track-level features

PNG's of exploratory visualizations and other results

Source Datasets:

Hugging Face. (2025). Spotify Tracks Dataset [Data set]. https://huggingface.co/datasets/maharshipandya/spotify-tracks-dataset


Kaggle. (2022). Million Song Dataset (subset) [Data set]
https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/sansastark/subset-of-the-million-song-dataset

Rights:
The dataset contains no personal data. It includes only audio-derived features and track metadata and complies with licensing for academic reuse.
